        "title": "Color and Perception",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The single most consequential fact in rendering color: **lighting math must happen in\nlinear light**, but **storage and display are perceptually (gamma) encoded**. Getting the\nencode/decode boundaries wrong is the most common correctness bug in graphics. This guide is\nthe bridge to `colors/` — that directory covers the full science of color; here we cover\nexactly what a renderer must get right."
    }
